---
title: Themes & Appearance
order: 5
description: Look-and-feel, Kvantum, icon themes, cursor themes, GTK theming
tags: [themes, kvantum, icons, cursor, gtk, appearance, plasma-style]
---

Plasma theming covers global themes, Plasma style, colors, icons, cursors, Kvantum, and GTK integration.

@text
Global Theme (Look and Feel)

A global theme bundles Plasma style, colors, icons, cursors, wallpaper, and splash screen.

@code bash
# List installed global themes
ls /usr/share/plasma/look-and-feel/
ls ~/.local/share/plasma/look-and-feel/

# Apply a global theme
plasma-apply-lookandfeel -l org.kde.breezedark.desktop

# List available global themes (by package name)
plasma-apply-lookandfeel --list

# Install a theme from a file
plasmapkg2 -t lookandfeel -i /path/to/theme.tar.gz

# Plasma 6
kpackagetool6 -t Plasma/LookAndFeel -i /path/to/theme.tar.gz

@text
Plasma Style (Desktop Theme)

Controls the appearance of panels, widgets, tooltips, and the system tray.

@code bash
# List installed Plasma styles
ls /usr/share/plasma/desktoptheme/
ls ~/.local/share/plasma/desktoptheme/

# Apply a Plasma style
plasma-apply-desktoptheme breeze-dark

# Install a Plasma style
plasmapkg2 -t theme -i /path/to/desktoptheme.tar.gz

@text
Color Scheme

@code bash
# List installed color schemes
ls /usr/share/color-schemes/
ls ~/.local/share/color-schemes/

# Apply a color scheme
plasma-apply-colorscheme BreezeDark

# List available color schemes
plasma-apply-colorscheme --list-schemes

# Install a color scheme (just copy the .colors file)
cp MyScheme.colors ~/.local/share/color-schemes/

@text
Icon Theme

@code bash
# List installed icon themes
ls /usr/share/icons/
ls ~/.local/share/icons/

# Set icon theme via config
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group Icons --key Theme "Papirus-Dark"

# Apply and reload (Plasma 5)
# After changing, reconfigure running apps:
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

# Install icon theme from package
sudo pacman -S papirus-icon-theme

# Install manually
tar xf icon-theme.tar.gz -C ~/.local/share/icons/
gtk-update-icon-cache ~/.local/share/icons/ThemeName/

@text
Cursor Theme

@code bash
# List installed cursor themes
ls /usr/share/icons/*/cursors 2>/dev/null | sed 's|/cursors||;s|.*/||'
ls ~/.local/share/icons/*/cursors 2>/dev/null | sed 's|/cursors||;s|.*/||'

# Apply a cursor theme
plasma-apply-cursortheme Breeze_Snow

# List available cursor themes
plasma-apply-cursortheme --list-themes

# Set cursor size
kwriteconfig5 --file kcminputrc --group Mouse --key cursorSize 32

# Set cursor theme for X11 fallback (add to ~/.Xresources)
# Xcursor.theme: Breeze_Snow
# Xcursor.size: 32
# Then: xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources

@text
Kvantum — Qt Theme Engine

Kvantum provides SVG-based Qt theming with blur, transparency, and custom widgets.

@code bash
# Install Kvantum
sudo pacman -S kvantum

# Set Qt style to Kvantum
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group KDE --key widgetStyle kvantum

# Open Kvantum Manager GUI
kvantummanager

# Set a Kvantum theme via CLI config
# Themes are in /usr/share/Kvantum/ or ~/.config/Kvantum/
# Active theme set in ~/.config/Kvantum/kvantum.kvconfig:
# [General]
# theme=KvArcDark

# Install a Kvantum theme
mkdir -p ~/.config/Kvantum/
cp -r /path/to/KvTheme ~/.config/Kvantum/

@text
GTK Theme Integration

Make GTK apps (Firefox, GIMP, etc.) match the Plasma appearance.

@code bash
# Install GTK Breeze theme
sudo pacman -S breeze-gtk

# Set GTK2 theme (~/.gtkrc-2.0)
# gtk-theme-name="Breeze-Dark"
# gtk-icon-theme-name="breeze-dark"
# gtk-cursor-theme-name="Breeze_Snow"
# gtk-font-name="Noto Sans 10"

# Set GTK3 theme (~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini)
# [Settings]
# gtk-theme-name=Breeze-Dark
# gtk-icon-theme-name=breeze-dark
# gtk-cursor-theme-name=Breeze_Snow
# gtk-font-name=Noto Sans 10
# gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme=true

# Set GTK4 theme
# Same as GTK3, in ~/.config/gtk-4.0/settings.ini

# Plasma's GTK settings module handles this automatically:
kcmshell5 kcm_style        # includes GTK tab

# Force GTK theme via environment
# export GTK_THEME=Breeze-Dark

@text
Fonts

@code bash
# Set default fonts via config
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key font "Noto Sans,10,-1,5,50,0,0,0,0,0"
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key fixed "Hack,10,-1,5,50,0,0,0,0,0"

# Set font DPI
kwriteconfig5 --file kcmfonts --group General --key forceFontDPI 96

# Font anti-aliasing settings
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key XftAntialias true
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key XftHintStyle hintslight
kwriteconfig5 --file kdeglobals --group General --key XftSubPixel rgb

# Rebuild font cache after installing new fonts
fc-cache -fv

# List installed fonts matching a pattern
fc-list | grep -i "hack"
